No-UI Keychain query and decrypt-ACL preflight design references:
https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/tree/897bff3
Sources/CodexBarCore/KeychainNoUIQuery.swift
Sources/CodexBarCore/KeychainAccessPreflight.swift

A read without UI carries both the UI-fail policy and an LAContext with
interactionNotAllowed, and runs only after the item's decrypt access list is
found to admit this process's code signature. No token refresh, ACL change or
preauthorization is implemented, and Claude Code's refresh token is never
parsed, used or stored. Native Claude profile service selection was
independently checked against the installed Claude Code 2.1.311 bundle.

